nt is what makes the durable decision the authority ('that ERT assertion is the stale one, not the JVM's'). Pattern IF: 'A policy's decision depends on the state of something outside the process making the decision.' The clock the operator sees is decided inside Emacs by agent-chat.el's local floor-only rule, but the authority for that turn's clock is the durable :clock-decision in the JVM. Pattern HOWEVER: 'A local stand-in is cheaper and usually right, and it is wrong silently: it drifts exactly when the thing it stands in for has moved.' The buffer's local rule agrees with the resolver everywhere except the case the amendment changed: an operator turn that names a target while the buffer is clocked elsewhere. In that case the buffer shows M-old, the record says M-new, and nothing reports the difference. Pattern THEN: 'Name the authority, refresh or read it directly ... and fail on incomparability'. For operator turns the buffer takes its clock from the durable decision returned for that turn and does not re-derive it; when no decision is available it says so. Non-operator surfaces keep floor-only, which already agrees with the authority. The executable form of this comparison is the locator for this token: ERT agent-chat-clock-agrees-with-durable-decision, selected by exact name so that a missing test fails.", :response-id "response-eb3bcb9349ba3a79", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385264596-24590-15a4c0ed"}}, :coordination/session-durability-check {:request-id "request-8ab72109cbf6ba5a", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/session-durability-check.flexiarg", :sha256 "94ec03f3fe051f99e9d4dac39df9f3ac08140903ef17cf56372466000b294e88"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern covers durability only. The criterion's other clauses come from elsewhere: coverage of every surface, the vocabulary for the negative decision (apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure), and idempotent retry (social/idempotent-handoff). 'Verify durability at G0' names futon3's proof-path gate stages, which have no counterpart in clock admission beyond 'before the agent runs'. The pattern also does not fill the gaps I noted in the locator. The retry and failure assertions use the in-memory store rather than the real backend, and each surface is exercised with one turn rather than a multi-turn session.", :want :exit/h59adca2cd730, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :coordination/session-durability-check :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :beyond-horizon} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :beyond-horizon}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :o