ed case ends in a refusal. The fact currently reads false because its locator (a registered futon3c.agency.clock-decision-test run, including ^:slow tests) has not been registered yet. Line 4 of the mission says this exit was satisfied at DERIVE/INSTANTIATE-1.", :response-id "response-75f7af70cbde280f", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790384990445-24583-69181b7d"}}, :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts {:request-id "request-750ea9b37bcb0ea0", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts.flexiarg", :sha256 "adf92965b95ce5487a2d0a50654d531ff13a4c9ab67bb86aed3045277cccefeb"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern does not cover clause 2 (single-active: switch, never stack). The sidecar promotes into a set of facts and has no rule for one fact replacing another. The pattern's promotion is an act someone performs explicitly, not the operator's one-key confirm or hydra override. Automatic promotion that passes the gate and is logged satisfies the pattern, but only the witnessed-and-auditable half of clause 3, not the confirmable half. The 'ideally XTDB' existence witness does not carry over, and neither do the sidecar's SQLite, enum and score-bound checks.", :want :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 23.36816913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 0.875, :g-comparison {:delta 0.875, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 0.875, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :no-producer}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts], :status :already-ordered}], :kind :machine-constructed, :checks-added [], :no-move-findings nil, :order {:units [{:unit :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :pattern :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point} {:unit :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts]], :meets {[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:11:01.927543409Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answers for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. A target mentioned in a turn is a proposal. The session's clock (turn→mission) is the authoritative fact. The pattern's rule is 'Promote proposals to facts only via explicit, logged actions': promotion goes through a validation gate and appends a promotion record, because 'Explicit promotion prevents silent contamination and preserves auditability'. Clause 1 of the criterion (resolves to a real existing target, not a fuzzy guess) is the validation gate: exact-token resolution against filesystem candidates, with no clock writes outside it. Clause 4 (audit trail) is the promotion record, which is the auto-clock-witness on the Emacs path and the durable :clock-decision on the JVM path. Clause 3's 'a witnessed proposal ... not an assertion' is the pattern's split between proposal and fact. The guard needs :exit/h1dae607747ce, which orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point produces in this context. Line 35 of the mission puts auto-promotion after the rule and the override surface are named ('Until then: manual clock-in + the hydra are the floor').", :response-id "response-d88ef783e61b36ae", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385046679-24584-f93198b0"}}, :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output {:request-id "request-46a6f3f653611603", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output.flexiarg", :sha256 "5d967af8172adde950488ed079771803a17667cb13d07f9d8fd7541c009bf3a1"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's fuzzy output is ANN/vector neighbours with scores, stored in SQLite with a propose/review CLI, and none of that carries over. The mission forbids scored fuzzy candidates from clocking at all, whereas the pattern allows a reviewed proposal to be promoted. The pattern does not say where the token boundary lies (case, prefix, bare slug, substring). That comes from the mission's exact-token rule, and the locator for this token (futon3c.agency.clock-decision-fuzzy-test, not yet written) is what would show it holds.", :want :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 23.11816913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.125, :g-comparison {:delta 1.125, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.125, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :reason :no-producer}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :status :already-ordered}], :kind :machine-constructed, :checks-added [], :no-move-findings nil, :order {:units [{:unit :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :pattern :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point} {:unit :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts} {:unit :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output, :pattern :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts]], :meets {[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:12:02.066942073Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answers for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The pattern's IF names the hazard in this criterion: fuzzy output 'used directly as facts or chain steps'. Here the fuzzy output is a prose mention that looks like a mission, and the fact it would corrupt is the turn's clock (turn→mission ground truth). The pattern's THEN is to record fuzzy results only as proposals, with their method and evidence, and never as authority. Applied here, a fuzzy or passing mention may be kept as turn-level mention-graph data (DERIVE Rule 0) but never sets the clock. With no explicit resolved target, the clock stays at [no mission]. That is the criterion's ordering: 'A wrong auto-clock is worse than [no mission]'. An unpromoted proposal costs a missed clock, while a promoted fuzzy one corrupts the record. The pattern's BECAUSE ('preserves provenance and enables explicit promotion') is why the mention is kept rather than dropped: it stays diagnosable, and an explicit rule can promote it later.", :response-id "response-9d4c94d8991db9be", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385106862-24586-61928648"}}, :process/spec-drift-by-displacement {:request-id "request-4a8559ab33b4b7c2", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/process/spec-drift-by-displacement.flexiarg", :sha256 "7b41395c3703ff5bdc288c85fdbb2b1746438294cdef82594a568b75b97b2edd"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern concerns plans and specifications being displaced by newer artifacts, and its receipts (DRIFT-2026-09-05, the APM park-sink vocabulary) do not carry over. What carries over is the principle: only an authored decision may replace the source of truth, applied here to a runtime value rather than a document. The pattern does not decide that the operator is the author of the clock and bell senders are not; the mission does (Joe 2026-06-03, claude-8 2026-09-24). Explicit dispatch --mission is also an authored decision, and INSTANTIATE-5 keeps it authoritative. The amendment's 'dispatch turn never switches' can therefore only cover prose mentions in a dispatched prompt, and no test covers that case yet.", :want :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :status :already-ordered}], :kind :machine-constructed, :checks-added [], :no-move-findings nil, :order {:units [{:unit :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :pattern :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point} {:unit :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts} {:unit :process/spec-drift-by-displacement, :pattern :process/spec-drift-by-displacement} {:unit :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output, :pattern :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts]], :meets {[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:13:13.753764210Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answer for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The amendment divides turns by who wrote them, and the pattern says why that division is right: 'nothing replaces a typed source of truth without an author-authored decision', enforced by a boundary that refuses anything else, separating a decision from a mere change. The session's clock is a typed source of truth: turn→mission attribution that other work builds on. An operator turn naming an exact target is an author-authored decision, because the operator holds the clock, can see it, and is changing it. So the resolver switches (exact-mention-overrides-stale-clock-and-refusals-keep-it). A bell, auto-bellback or dispatch-prose mention is displacement: the clock would be replaced without any actor deciding to replace it. That is what happened when bellbacks mentioning M-futon-seams kept moving a seat's E-cascade-real clock. The refusing boundary is what bell-mentions-fill-an-empty-clock-but-do-not-switch pins: an empty clock may be filled, an occupied one is never switched. It also covers 'an ambiguous or unresolvable name records its refusal and leaves the clock where it was', since that refusal is itself recorded as a decision (kept-because). The pattern's T2a (drift goes where the checker has no jurisdiction) points at the Consequence paragraph: the Emacs buffer is outside the resolver's jurisdiction and still applies the old floor-only rule to operator input.", :response-id "response-f7d6b56cb137b171", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385174034-24587-deaf9fa2"}}, :hygiene/observe-the-authority {:request-id "request-69bbac2e9ce5cf1d", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/hygiene/observe-the-authority.flexiarg", :sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's own settings (buffer cleaning, repository hygiene, test-registry environments) do not carry over, and neither does its instruction to 'emit raw signals'. What carries over is the general move of reading the authority instead of trusting the stand-in. The ERT test checks that the buffer adopts the returned decision. It does not re-check the resolver, which clock-decision-test covers. The pattern also does not choose which side is the authority; the mission's amendment makes that choice.", :want :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :beyond-horizon}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-f