s an accounting failure, not reported as a successful recorded decision' is the pattern's 'reject success when persistence fails'. It closes the accepted-but-not-stored case, where an agent turn runs even though its clock decision silently failed to persist. 'Every accepted turn must have a persisted decision' is the gate itself: admission waits for durability. 'Keep absence and storage failure distinct' stops a lost write from being recorded as a legitimate :unclocked. The matching checks are complete-session-decisions-roundtrip-real-backend, persistence-failure-prevents-agent-execution and swallowed-callback-accounting-failure-fails-the-session.", :response-id "response-c33ca1e6c97b1e2a", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385510981-24593-3b10fbbb"}}, :process/spec-silence-pair {:request-id "request-6308ab6cd962e39d", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/process/spec-silence-pair.flexiarg", :sha256 "cbc8caba727aae873c8ea765bc1e384fe3886812df02f8cc4e431d8dc95c075a"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern concerns specifications and the agents acting on them. Its receipts (the APM park-path deletion, the U54 census form, the DRIFT account) and its refusal of deletions warranted by containment searches do not carry over. What carries over is how an absence claim must be recorded, applied to a runtime decision record instead of a reading of a spec. The pattern does not choose the reason keywords or the required fields; those come from the mission text.", :want :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:process/spec-silence-pair :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :coordination/session-durability-check :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :pr