ced'. The mission's clause 3 (line 21) is stricter and wants a surfaced, confirmable proposal, so this pattern supports 'never silent' only in the sense of always auditable. The NAG machinery (needs-you.edn, :fork-warrant, the latency and rubber-stamp metrics, the rule-to-pattern data table) does not carry over. The pattern also says nothing about exact-token resolution or existence witnesses; those come from the mission's principle #8. The retrieval candidate fulab/clock-in exists only as an @arg inside fulab/fulab-patterns.multiarg, so it has no .flexiarg path I could cite, and it concerns declaring a clock-in rather than inferring one.", :want :exit/h1dae607747ce, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 23.74316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 0.5, :g-comparison {:delta 0.5, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 0.5, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :no-producer}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by