roduces :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 in this context, the guard carries both dependencies the mission states. :exit/h59adca2cd730 comes from line 529: acceptance must construct the current bad case. :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 comes from lines 521-523: the negative case is the typed :unclocked/reason decision. The pattern holds that the commonest good outcome gets a first-class state in the primary record, written by one writer so that N consumers do not each reconstruct it. The 2026-09-21 diagnosis found that the commonest turn outcome, no inferable mission, had no state at all. An unclocked turn looked the same as a turn whose accounting never ran or had failed, with nil fields in every case, so each consumer had to guess which it was. The pattern's THEN, a distinct terminal state written when its evidence exists, is the criterion's explicit :unclocked/reason, recorded at turn admission. The admission contract across Emacs, bell and Marimo is the single writer, one resolver for every surface.", :response-id "response-b7be5b885a784db1", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790390021787-24641-3bc46a68"}}}}, :beta-declared 1, :habit 1.0, :habit-status :computed, :f nil, :f-status :not-supplied, :reason :no-admitted-policy-prefix, :f-prefix {:schema :wm/policy-prefix-evidence-v1, :policy {:kind :cascade-candidate, :id :C1, :target "M-autoclock-in", :precedence [{:id :process/spec-silence-pair, :authority :documented-interpretation, :produces #{["M-autoclock-in" :exit/h0f3acdf222d7]}, :guard {:status :interpreted, :operator :and, :clauses [{:status :interpreted, :present #{}, :absent #{}}]}, :transition {:status :interpreted, :operator :union, :produces #{["M-autoclock-in" :exit/h0f3acdf222d7]}, :authority :documented-interpretation}, :target "M-autoclock-in"} {:id :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :authority :documented-interpretation, :produces #{["M-autoclock-in" :exit/h1dae607747ce]}, :guard {:status :interpreted, :operator :and, :clauses [{:status :interpr