authority for that turn's clock is the durable :clock-decision in the JVM. Pattern HOWEVER: 'A local stand-in is cheaper and usually right, and it is wrong silently: it drifts exactly when the thing it stands in for has moved.' The buffer's local rule agrees with the resolver everywhere except the case the amendment changed: an operator turn that names a target while the buffer is clocked elsewhere. In that case the buffer shows M-old, the record says M-new, and nothing reports the difference. Pattern THEN: 'Name the authority, refresh or read it directly ... and fail on incomparability'. For operator turns the buffer takes its clock from the durable decision returned for that turn and does not re-derive it; when no decision is available it says so. Non-operator surfaces keep floor-only, which already agrees with the authority. The executable form of this comparison is the locator for this token: ERT agent-chat-clock-agrees-with-durable-decision, selected by exact name so that a missing test fails.", :response-id "response-eb3bcb9349ba3a79", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385264596-24590-15a4c0ed"}}, :coordination/session-durability-check {:request-id "request-8ab72109cbf6ba5a", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/session-durability-check.flexiarg", :sha256 "94ec03f3fe051f99e9d4dac39df9f3ac08140903ef17cf56372466000b294e88"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern covers durability only. The criterion's other clauses come from elsewhere: coverage of every surface, the vocabulary for the negative decision (apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure), and idempotent retry (social/idempotent-handoff). 'Verify durability at G0' names futon3's proof-path gate stages, which have no counterpart in clock admission beyond 'before the agent runs'. The pattern also does not fill the gaps I noted in the locator. The retry and failure assertions use the in-memory store rather than the real backend, and each surface is exercised with one turn rather than a multi-turn session.", :want :exit/h59adca2cd730, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :coordination/session-durability-check :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :beyond-horizon} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :beyond-horizon}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :hygiene/observe-the-authority :coordination/session-durability-check :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :coordination/session-durability-check :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :status :reordered}], :kind :machine-constructed, :checks-added [], :no-move-findings nil, :order {:units [{:unit :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :pattern :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point} {:unit :hygiene/observe-the-authority, :pattern :hygiene/observe-the-authority} {:unit :coordination/session-durability-check, :pattern :coordination/session-durability-check} {:unit :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts} {:unit :process/spec-drift-by-displacement, :pattern :process/spec-drift-by-displacement} {:unit :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output, :pattern :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] [:process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority]], :meets {[:hygiene/observe-the-authority :process/spec-drift-by-displacement] :hygiene/observe-the-authority, [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:18:51.177583439Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answer for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The pattern says to 'gate successful responses on durable persistence ... verify durability ... and reject success when persistence fails'. Its reasons are that 'acknowledging success before persistence creates silent loss modes (accepted-but-not-stored)' and that 'a proof-path is only real if it can be reconstructed later'. The acceptance criterion's clauses map onto it as follows. 'Read both cases back through a newly constructed real durable backend client' is the reconstruct-later test: the decisions have to survive outside the process that wrote them, not only in its cache. 'If recording fails, assert it is surfaced as an accounting failure, not reported as a successful recorded decision' is the pattern's 'reject success when persistence fails'. It closes the accepted-but-not-stored case, where an agent turn runs even though its clock decision silently failed to persist. 'Every accepted turn must have a persisted decision' is the gate itself: admission waits for durability. 'Keep absence and storage failure distinct' stops a lost write from being recorded as a legitimate :unclocked. The matching checks are complete-session-decisions-roundtrip-real-backend, persistence-failure-prevents-agent-execution and swallowed-callback-accounting-failure-fails-the-session.", :response-id "response-c33ca1e6c97b1e2a", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385510981-24593-3b10fbbb"}}, :process/spec-silence-pair {:request-id "request-6308ab6cd962e39d", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/process/spec-silence-pair.flexiarg", :sha256 "cbc8caba727aae873c8ea765bc1e384fe3886812df02f8cc4e431d8dc95c075a"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern concerns specifications and the agents acting on them. Its receipts (the APM park-path deletion, the U54 census form, the DRIFT account) and its refusal of deletions warranted by containment searches do not carry over. What carries over is how an absence claim must be recorded, applied to a runtime decision record instead of a reading of a spec. The pattern does not choose the reason keywords or the required fields; those come from the mission text.", :want :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :a