ccess before persistence creates silent loss modes (accepted-but-not-stored)' and that 'a proof-path is only real if it can be reconstructed later'. The acceptance criterion's clauses map onto it as follows. 'Read both cases back through a newly constructed real durable backend client' is the reconstruct-later test: the decisions have to survive outside the process that wrote them, not only in its cache. 'If recording fails, assert it is surfaced as an accounting failure, not reported as a successful recorded decision' is the pattern's 'reject success when persistence fails'. It closes the accepted-but-not-stored case, where an agent turn runs even though its clock decision silently failed to persist. 'Every accepted turn must have a persisted decision' is the gate itself: admission waits for durability. 'Keep absence and storage failure distinct' stops a lost write from being recorded as a legitimate :unclocked. The matching checks are complete-session-decisions-roundtrip-real-backend, persistence-failure-prevents-agent-execution and swallowed-callback-accounting-failure-fails-the-session.", :response-id "response-c33ca1e6c97b1e2a", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385510981-24593-3b10fbbb"}}, :process/spec-silence-pair {:request-id "request-6308ab6cd962e39d", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/process/spec-silence-pair.flexiarg", :sha256 "cbc8caba727aae873c8ea765bc1e384fe3886812df02f8cc4e431d8dc95c075a"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern concerns specifications and the agents acting on them. Its receipts (the APM park-path deletion, the U54 census form, the DRIFT account) and its refusal of deletions warranted by containment searches do not carry over. What carries over is how an absence claim must be recorded, applied to a runtime decision record instead of a reading of a spec. The pattern does not