ation-evidence-present (the terminal form of the held-out evidence this source already defines: observations collected, then calibrated). With today's evidence absent (all three evidence C3 locators false), the recheck observes the obstruction PRESENT and this cascade produces nothing further -- no false completion; if the evidence were already present, C1 correctly reaches acceptance on its short path. DECLARED EFFECT: produces exactly :repair/obstruction-observed-cleared, only when the held-out calibration evidence is present.", :scope-limit "Models the cleared branch, which the ticket's 'if it has cleared' route accepts directly. The still-present branch is NOT claimed as completion: if the recheck observes the obstruction present, this cascade stops after the observation and the ticket stays open for the restore route -- the kernel's guard chain simply does not reach acceptance, and no completion token is produced. A single declared-source pattern cannot carry both observation outcomes (the kernel transition is deterministic, cascade_model_manifest.clj:282); the present-branch is therefore represented by NOT reaching the terminal, which is exactly the ticket's semantics.", :target-source {:repo "futon2", :path "holes/tickets/T-repair-occ-444fb018cbbb656d09b8f4f67c063f1d51a1932a9b1c281d999c567cf22a2ade.md", :section "Scoped task"}, :observation-limit "C4 observes the record's DISPOSITION LINE: the recheck record must carry a line starting RECHECK-DISPOSITION-CLEARED, written only when the dated check observed the obstruction cleared; a record whose disposition line reads RECHECK-DISPOSITION-PRESENT does not satisfy this token (decl-present?'s token boundary rejects differing heads)."}, :apparatus/evidence-to-disposition-once {:kind :hand-admitted, :by "zai-1", :date "2026-09-22", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/evidence-to-disposition-once.flexiarg", :sha256 "9f6b75df557cb3475b320fba4c73f02761702b088ba3c7ca13aa99e666bba764"}, :reading "The ticket's 'if it has cleared, retain a dated recheck' branch: the dated observation IS the disposition; acceptance converts it once into the ticket's DONE state. DECLARED EFFECT: produces exactly :restoration-accepted from :repair/obstruction-observed-cleared.", :scope-limit "Only the cleared-branch acceptance. Does not accept on a present-observation or on any declaration.", :target-source {:repo "futon2", :path "holes/tickets/T-repair-occ-444fb018cbbb656d09b8f4f67c063f1d51a1932a9b1c281d999c567cf22a2ade.md", :section "Acceptance evidence"}, :observation-limit "C4 observes the ticket's Status line reading DONE; ordinary ticket review guards the transition."}, :aif/declare-the-conditioning {:kind :hand-admitted, :by "zai-1", :date "2026-09-22", :source {:path "futon3/library/aif/declare-the-conditioning.flexiarg", :sha256 "a70bdf4d1c172246503a1a3a55748e4362d1faeba56025b01d54980f25783135"}, :reading "The restore branch begins by declaring the held-out split before any outcomes exist. DECLARED EFFECT: produces exactly :repair/split-declared-valid -- a valid preregistered split declaration. The declaration ENABLES collecting prospective observations; it supplies no evidence itself.", :scope-limit "One declaration resource. Does not collect observations, does not calibrate, does not restore, does not satisfy the ticket by existing.", :target-source {:repo "futon2", :path "holes/tickets/T-repair-occ-444fb018cbbb656d09b8f4f67c063f1d51a1932a9b1c281d999c567cf22a2ade.md", :section "Scoped task"}, :observation-limit "C4 observes the declaration's DISPOSITION LINE: HELD-OUT-SPLIT-DECLARED is written only when the split parses with its required fields (locator, held-out set, no-result/failure/timeout classes); a malformed declaration carries no such line and the token stays false."}, :aif/measurement-window-hygiene {:kind :hand-admitted, :by "zai-1", :date "2026-09-22", :source {:path "futon3/library/aif/measurement-window-hygiene.flexiarg", :sha256 "0d90eac2b154faf3a463ea7c20f7b597f44fee80b25