turn/job id and time. The pattern also separates a search that ran and found nothing from a search that could not run. The criterion names the same split: Distinguish a known absence from an unavailable dependency. Every source consulted and none matching is a known absence. An unreadable holes root, or an activity or store feed that throws, is not established, and needs its own reason. Folding it into :no-source would create exactly the false known the pattern warns about. The typed reasons for ambiguous candidates and for an unresolved explicit target follow the pattern's instruction to treat unspecified behaviour as a finding to route to a decision, not as a licence. Do not silently preserve a stale unrelated target or invent a mission covers both halves of the pair. Inventing a mission lets unspecified behaviour accrete (T4a). Silently keeping a stale target reads silence as consent to the old clock. The resolver has no unavailable-evidence reason today, so the criterion reads false. Its locator is futon3c.agency.clock-decision-reasons-test, which is not yet written.", :response-id "response-363c69f83c37109a", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790389067129-24632-68e02385"}}, :apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure {:request-id "request-e2e7978b74b4aa5a", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure.flexiarg", :sha256 "5dce45ef7c2d1e4c8221d1a2156976f822d37fec561a6ad5a4aa18f14d852ba7"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's example is the reverse case: there, success was recorded in fault vocabulary. Here a legitimate negative outcome had no vocabulary at all and looked like a gap. The principle carries over; the APM wrapper and cancellation details do not. The idempotency clause (stable turn/job identity) comes from social/idempotent-handoff, not from this pattern. D