ion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts]], :meets {[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:11:01.927543409Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answers for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. A target mentioned in a turn is a proposal. The session's clock (turn→mission) is the authoritative fact. The pattern's rule is 'Promote proposals to facts only via explicit, logged actions': promotion goes through a validation gate and appends a promotion record, because 'Explicit promotion prevents silent contamination and preserves auditability'. Clause 1 of the criterion (resolves to a real existing target, not a fuzzy guess) is the validation gate: exact-token resolution against filesystem candidates, with no clock writes outside it. Clause 4 (audit trail) is the promotion record, which is the auto-clock-witness on the Emacs path and the durable :clock-decision on the JVM path. Clause 3's 'a witnessed proposal ... not an assertion' is the pattern's split between proposal and fact. The guard needs :exit/h1dae607747ce, which orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point produces in this context. Line 35 of the mission puts auto-promotion after the rule and the override surface are named ('Until then: manual clock-in + the hydra are the floor').", :response-id "response-d88ef783e61b36ae", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385046679-24584-f93198b0"}}, :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output {:request-id "request-46a6f3f653611603", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output.flexiarg", :sha256 "5d967af8172adde950488ed079771803a17667cb13d07f9d8fd7541c009bf3a1"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's fuzzy output is ANN/vector neighbours with scores, stored in SQLite with a propose/review CLI, and none of that carries over. The mission forbids scored fuzzy candidates from clocking at all, whereas the pattern allows a reviewed proposal to be promoted. The pattern does not say where the token boundary lies (case, prefix, bare slug, substring). That comes from the mission's exact-token rule, and the locator for this token (futon3c.agency.clock-decision-fuzzy-test, not yet written) is what would show it holds.", :want :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 23.11816913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.125, :g-comparison {:delta 1.125, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.125, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :reason :no-producer}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :status :already-ordered}], :kind :machine-constructed, :checks-added [], :no-move-findings nil, :order {:units [{:unit :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :pattern :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point} {:unit :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts} {:unit :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output, :pattern :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts]], :meets {[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:12:02.066942073Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answers for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The pattern's IF names the hazard in this criterion: fuzzy output 'used directly as facts or chain steps'. Here the fuzzy output is a prose mention that looks like a mission, and the fact it would corrupt is the turn's clock (turn→mission ground truth). The pattern's THEN is to record fuzzy results only as proposals, with their method and evidence, and never as authority. Applied here, a fuzzy or passing mention may be kept as turn-level mention-graph data (DERIVE Rule 0) but never sets the clock. With no explicit resolved target, the clock stays at [no mission]. That is the criterion's ordering: 'A wrong auto-clock is worse than [no mission]'. An unpromoted proposal costs a missed clock, while a promoted fuzzy one corrupts the record. The pattern's BECAUSE ('preserves provenance and enables explicit promotion') is why the mention is kept rather than dropped: it stays diagnosable, and an explicit rule can promote it later.", :response-id "response-9d4c94d8991db9be", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385106862-24586-61928648"}}, :process/spec-drift-by-displacement {:request-id "request-4a8559ab33b4b7c2", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/process/spec-drift-by-displacement.flexiarg", :sha256 "7b41395c3703ff5bdc288c85fdbb2b1746438294cdef82594a568b75b97b2edd"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern concerns plans and specifications being displaced by newer artifacts, and its receipts (DRIFT-2026-09-05, the APM park-sink vocabulary) do not carry over. What carries over is the principle: only an authored decision may replace the source of truth, applied here to a runtime value rather than a document. The pattern does not decide that the operator is the author of the clock and bell senders are not; the mission does (Joe 2026-06-03, claude-8 2026-09-24). Explicit dispatch --mission is also an authored decision, and INSTANTIATE-5 keeps it authoritative. The amendment's 'dispatch turn never switches' can therefore only cover prose mentions in a dispatched prompt, and no test covers that case yet.", :want :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :tok