 {[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:13:13.753764210Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answer for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The amendment divides turns by who wrote them, and the pattern says why that division is right: 'nothing replaces a typed source of truth without an author-authored decision', enforced by a boundary that refuses anything else, separating a decision from a mere change. The session's clock is a typed source of truth: turn→mission attribution that other work builds on. An operator turn naming an exact target is an author-authored decision, because the operator holds the clock, can see it, and is changing it. So the resolver switches (exact-mention-overrides-stale-clock-and-refusals-keep-it). A bell, auto-bellback or dispatch-prose mention is displacement: the clock would be replaced without any actor deciding to replace it. That is what happened when bellbacks mentioning M-futon-seams kept moving a seat's E-cascade-real clock. The refusing boundary is what bell-mentions-fill-an-empty-clock-but-do-not-switch pins: an empty clock may be filled, an occupied one is never switched. It also covers 'an ambiguous or unresolvable name records its refusal and leaves the clock where it was', since that refusal is itself recorded as a decision (kept-because). The pattern's T2a (drift goes where the checker has no jurisdiction) points at the Consequence paragraph: the Emacs buffer is outside the resolver's jurisdiction and still applies the old floor-only rule to operator input.", :response-id "response-f7d6b56cb137b171", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385174034-24587-deaf9fa2"}}, :hygiene/observe-the-authority {:request-id "request-69bbac2e9ce5cf1d", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/hygiene/observe-the-authority.flexiarg", :sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's own settings (buffer cleaning, repository hygiene, test-registry environments) do not carry over, and neither does its instruction to 'emit raw signals'. What carries over is the general move of reading the authority instead of trusting the stand-in. The ERT test checks that the buffer adopts the returned decision. It does not re-check the resolver, which clock-decision-test covers. The pattern also does not choose which side is the authority; the mission's amendment makes that choice.", :want :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :beyond-horizon}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reason :no-admitted-move, :horizon 4, :search {:expanded 9, :limit 20000}, :ordering [{:move-id :order-by-need, :before [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :after [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :status :reordered}], :kind :machine-constructed, :checks-added [], :no-move-findings nil, :order {:units [{:unit :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point, :pattern :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point} {:unit :hygiene/observe-the-authority, :pattern :hygiene/observe-the-authority} {:unit :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts, :pattern :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts} {:unit :process/spec-drift-by-displacement, :pattern :process/spec-drift-by-displacement} {:unit :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output, :pattern :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output}], :descent [[:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] [:process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority]], :meets {[:hygiene/observe-the-authority :process/spec-drift-by-displacement] :hygiene/observe-the-authority, [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:14:43.523872948Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answer for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The guard now needs :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, which process/spec-drift-by-displacement produces in this context. That matches the stated constraint: this criterion is the Consequence of the Rule 0 amendment, and the amendment is what makes the durable decision the authority ('that ERT assertion is the stale one, not the JVM's'). Pattern IF: 'A policy's decision depends on the state of something outside the process making the decision.' The clock the operator sees is decided inside Emacs by agent-chat.el's local floor-only rule, but the authority for that turn's clock is the durable :clock-decision in the JVM. Pattern HOWEVER: 'A local stand-in is cheaper and usually right, and it is wrong silently: it drifts exactly when the thing it stands in for has moved.' The buffer's local rule agrees with the resolver everywhere except the case the amendment changed: an operator turn that names a target while the buffer is clocked elsewhere. In that case the buffer shows M-old, the record says M-new, and nothing reports the difference. Pattern THEN: 'Name the authority, refresh or read it directly ... and fail on incomparability'. For operator turns the buffer takes its clock from the durable decision returned for that turn and does not re-derive it; when no decision is available it says so. Non-operator surfaces keep floor-only, which already agrees with the authority. The executable form of this comparison is the locator for this token: ERT agent-chat-clock-agrees-with-durable-decision, selected by exact name so that a missing test fails.", :response-id "response-eb3bcb9349ba3a79", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385264596-24590-15a4c0ed"}}, :coordination/session-durability-check {:request-id "request-8ab72109cbf6ba5a", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/session-durability-check.flexiarg", :sha256 "94ec03f3fe051f99e9d4dac39df9f3ac08140903ef17cf56372466000b294e88"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern covers durability only. The criterion's other clauses come from elsewhere: coverage of every surface, the vocabulary for the negative decision (apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure), and idempotent retry (social/idempotent-handoff). 'Verify durability at G0' names futon3's proof-path gate stages, which have no counterpart in clock admission beyond 'before the agent runs'. The pattern also does not fill the gaps I noted in the locator. The retry and failure assertions use the in-memory store rather than the real backend, and each surface is exercised with one turn rather than a multi-turn session.", :want :exit/h59adca2cd730, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :coordination/session-durability-check :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :beyond-horizon} {:t