:target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:10:05.498520876Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answers for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged (sha rechecked this session). The IDENTIFY exit asks for a resolution rule and an override surface, named together so that a mislabel can never be silent. The pattern treats a choice-point as having two faces. When the rule decides the case (an exact token resolves to one existing target, and Rule 0 is scoped by who wrote the turn, per the 2026-09-25 amendment), the clock change is an autonomous pick that carries its warrant: the durable :clock-decision with its source, tokens, and old and new target. When the rule cannot decide (the name is ambiguous, unresolvable, or several targets sit at one level), it must not guess. It records a typed refusal, and the operator's hydra stays available as the smallest way to unblock. The criterion's floor, 'Until then: manual clock-in + the hydra are the floor', is the pattern's DOES-NOT-APPLY clause: where no signed-off rule exists, write the rule first and do not warrant anything. The exit holds when both faces are named and pinned, because then every clock change carries a warrant and every undecided case ends in a refusal. The fact currently reads false because its locator (a registered futon3c.agency.clock-decision-test run, including ^:slow tests) has not been registered yet. Line 4 of the mission says this exit was satisfied at DERIVE/INSTANTIATE-1.", :response-id "response-75f7af70cbde280f", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790384990445-24583-69181b7d"}}, :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts {:request-id "request-750ea9b37bcb0ea0", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts.flexiarg", :sha256 "adf92965b95ce5487a2d0a50654d531ff13a4c9ab67bb86aed3045277cccefeb"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern does not cover clause 2 (single-active: switch, never stack). The sidecar promotes into a set of facts and has no rule for one fact replacing another. The pattern's promotion is an act someone performs explicitly, not the operator's one-key confirm or hydra override. Automatic promotion that passes the gate and is logged satisfies the pattern, but only the witnessed-and-auditable half of clause 3, not the confirmable half. The 'ideally XTDB' existence witness does not carry over, and neither do the sidecar's SQLite, enum and score-bound checks.", :want :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 23.36816913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 0.875, :g-comparison {:delta 0.875, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 0.875, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :reason :no-producer}], :coverage {:moves-taken [:compose-by-need], :final-evaluation {}}, :stop-reaso