point produces in this context. Line 35 of the mission puts auto-promotion after the rule and the override surface are named ('Until then: manual clock-in + the hydra are the floor').", :response-id "response-d88ef783e61b36ae", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385046679-24584-f93198b0"}}, :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output {:request-id "request-46a6f3f653611603", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output.flexiarg", :sha256 "5d967af8172adde950488ed079771803a17667cb13d07f9d8fd7541c009bf3a1"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's fuzzy output is ANN/vector neighbours with scores, stored in SQLite with a propose/review CLI, and none of that carries over. The mission forbids scored fuzzy candidates from clocking at all, whereas the pattern allows a reviewed proposal to be promoted. The pattern does not say where the token boundary lies (case, prefix, bare slug, substring). That comes from the mission's exact-token rule, and the locator for this token (futon3c.agency.clock-decision-fuzzy-test, not yet written) is what would show it holds.", :want :exit/h7afd70f40a29, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 23.11816913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.125, :g-comparison {:delta 1.125, :universe