ilable-evidence reason today, so the criterion reads false. Its locator is futon3c.agency.clock-decision-reasons-test, which is not yet written.", :response-id "response-363c69f83c37109a", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790389067129-24632-68e02385"}}, :apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure {:request-id "request-e2e7978b74b4aa5a", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure.flexiarg", :sha256 "5dce45ef7c2d1e4c8221d1a2156976f822d37fec561a6ad5a4aa18f14d852ba7"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's example is the reverse case: there, success was recorded in fault vocabulary. Here a legitimate negative outcome had no vocabulary at all and looked like a gap. The principle carries over; the APM wrapper and cancellation details do not. The idempotency clause (stable turn/job identity) comes from social/idempotent-handoff, not from this pattern. Durability is checked by the ^:slow real-backend roundtrip in futon3c.agency.clock-decision-test.", :want :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:process/spec-silence-pair :orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :coordination/session-durability-check :apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:mo